    "merge_intervals": "Return only one fenced Python code block, with imports and the requested function, no tests, no main block, and no explanation. Implement merge_intervals(intervals). Accept an iterable of (start, end) pairs of integers. Reject start > end with ValueError. Return a sorted list of tuples, merging overlapping closed intervals (including shared endpoints). Do not merge disjoint adjacent integer intervals, so (1,2) and (3,4) remain separate. Do not mutate the input. Empty input returns [].",
    "topological_sort": "Return only one fenced Python code block with imports and the requested function, no tests, no main block, no explanation. Implement topological_sort(nodes, edges) for integer node labels and directed (source,target) edges. Include isolated nodes. Ignore duplicate nodes and duplicate edges. Return the lexicographically smallest valid topological ordering. Raise ValueError if an edge endpoint is not in nodes or if a cycle exists. Do not mutate inputs.",
    "varint": "Return only one fenced Python code block with imports and two functions, no tests, no main block, no explanation. Implement encode_varint(value) -> bytes and decode_varint(data, offset=0) -> (value, next_offset) for unsigned 64-bit base-128 little-endian varints. Encoding accepts integers from 0 through 2**64-1; reject others with ValueError. Decoding accepts bytes, starts at a nonnegative offset, consumes exactly one varint and leaves trailing bytes. Raise ValueError for truncated, overflow, more than 10 bytes, an out-of-range offset, or noncanonical encodings (e.g. b'\\x80\\x00'). The canonical encoding of zero is b'\\x00'."
  },
